:::tab-content[tab=main width=880 align=center]

::::toolbar
- text[value="Report a bug"]
::::

::::form[name=report-bug submit="Send report" action=/report-bug]
- Title (text, "One line — what went wrong")
- What happened (textarea, "What did you see?")
- Expected (textarea, "What did you expect instead?")
- Steps to reproduce (textarea, "1. … 2. … (optional)")
::::

## What we will attach

::::row[icon=doc action=none href=#]
The page you came from
Its path and the surface name
::::

::::row[icon=doc action=none href=#]
Your browser window
Viewport size, light or dark, language and time zone
::::

::::row[icon=doc action=none href=#]
The build you are on
The running server version
::::

::::row[icon=doc action=none href=#]
Recent console errors and warnings
The last 50 lines, with tokens, keys, passwords and cookies removed
::::

:::

::

The screenshot picker is a single optional image (PNG, JPEG or WebP, up to 10 MB) spliced into the form above the submit — surf-parse has no file field kind. A refused file never costs the report: the row saves and the page comes back with an honest banner about the file alone.

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — deferred"]
The "What we will attach" rows are a read-only manifest, not controls. They render as rows because the form grammar has no static description-list item today; `action=none` marks them inert.
::
